            <div xml:id="d336">

                <pb facs="0649" n="529" sameAs="frus:frus1932v01/pg529"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A4 Naval Armaments/135: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Delegate to the Bureau of the General
                        Disarmament Conference (Wilson) to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-10-03T22:00:00+01:00">October 3, 1932—10
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 3—5:43 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>397. From Davis. Simon, who must return to London tomorrow stopping for a
                    conversation with Herriot in Paris, has asked me to come to London the end of
                    this week to take up the naval conversations. We therefore plan to leave here
                    Thursday.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
